---
import Toc from '../Toc.astro';
import { can } from '~/lib/roles';
import type { HelpReader } from '~/lib/help';

type Props = { reader: HelpReader };
const { reader } = Astro.props;
const isMaster = can(reader, 'people');
---

<Toc
  items={[
    { id: 'rules', label: 'Five rules' },
    { id: 'password', label: 'Your password' },
    { id: 'authenticator', label: 'The authenticator app' },
    { id: 'recovery', label: 'Recovery codes' },
    { id: 'customer-details', label: 'Customers’ details' },
    { id: 'suspicious', label: 'If something looks wrong' },
  ]}
/>

<section id="rules" aria-labelledby="rules-h">
  <h2 id="rules-h">Five rules</h2>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" data-remember="safe-own" />
        <span>
          <strong>One person, one account.</strong>
          <small>Never share your password or your authenticator. The activity log records every change under your name.</small>
        </span>
      </label>
    </li>
    <li>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" data-remember="safe-ask" />
        <span>
          <strong>Nobody from Nepsemyak will ask for your code or password.</strong>
          <small>Not by phone, email, WhatsApp or chat. Anyone who asks is not us: say no and tell the master admin.</small>
        </span>
      </label>
    </li>
    <li>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" data-remember="safe-shared" />
        <span>
          <strong>On shared office computers, don’t let the browser save your password, and sign out when you finish.</strong>
          <small><span class="ui">Sign out</span> is at the top right of every admin page.</small>
        </span>
      </label>
    </li>
    <li>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" data-remember="safe-codes" />
        <span>
          <strong>Recovery codes stay on paper or in a password manager.</strong>
          <small>Not in email, WhatsApp or your phone’s photos.</small>
        </span>
      </label>
    </li>
    <li>
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" data-remember="safe-suspect" />
        <span>
          <strong>If you think someone knows your password, change it at once.</strong>
          <small>Changing it signs out every other device. Then tell the master admin.</small>
        </span>
      </label>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="password" aria-labelledby="password-h">
  <h2 id="password-h">Your password</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li>At least 10 characters. A few unrelated words (“mango bicycle Tuesday river”) are strong and easy to remember.</li>
    <li>Change it under <span class="ui">My account</span> → <span class="ui">Password</span>. Every other device is signed out when you do.</li>
    <li>Forgotten it? On the sign-in page choose <span class="ui">Forgot password?</span>; a code is emailed to you. You still need the authenticator afterwards, so someone who gets into your email alone can’t get in.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="authenticator" aria-labelledby="authenticator-h">
  <h2 id="authenticator-h">The authenticator app</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li>The 6-digit code changes every 30 seconds. Type it before it changes.</li>
    <li>The panel asks for a fresh code every 12 hours, and whenever you sign in on a new device.</li>
    <li>
      Getting a new phone? Before you reset the old one, ask {isMaster ? 'the website developer' : 'the master admin'} to reset
      your two-step sign-in, then scan a new QR code at your next sign-in.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="recovery" aria-labelledby="recovery-h">
  <h2 id="recovery-h">Recovery codes</h2>
  <p>
    You got 10 when you set up the authenticator. Each works once, in place of the app code, if your phone is lost or broken.
    When three or fewer are left, the dashboard reminds you: make a fresh set under <span class="ui">My account</span> →
    <span class="ui">Create new recovery codes</span>. The old ones stop working.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="customer-details" aria-labelledby="customer-h">
  <h2 id="customer-h">Customers’ details</h2>
  <p>
    Queries contain people’s names, phone numbers, addresses and complaints. Use them only to answer the query. Don’t copy them
    into personal chats, share screenshots outside the office, or forward alert emails to anyone who isn’t on the team.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="suspicious" aria-labelledby="suspicious-h">
  <h2 id="suspicious-h">If something looks wrong</h2>
  <p>
    A change you didn’t make, a sign-in you don’t recognise, or a code you didn’t ask for: change your password, then tell the
    master admin straight away.
    {isMaster && ' As master, you can sign anyone out on every device under Users, and see every sign-in and change under Activity.'}
  </p>
</section>
